---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "May 11, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Envelope" description="How Envelope handles your data.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 prose-envelope">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      Envelope ("we", "us") builds budgeting software. This policy explains what data we collect, why, and how we handle it. This document is a draft and should be reviewed by counsel before launch.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account data</strong> — email address and authentication identifiers when you sign in.</li>
      <li><strong>Budget data</strong> — envelopes, accounts, transactions, goals you create in the app. Stored encrypted at rest.</li>
      <li><strong>Diagnostic data</strong> — crash reports and anonymized usage events to improve the product.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not connect to your bank or request banking credentials.</li>
      <li>We do not sell your data.</li>
      <li>We do not show third-party ads.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use data</h2>
    <p>
      Account data is used to authenticate you and sync your budget across devices. Budget data is stored only to provide the sync feature — it is encrypted in transit and at rest. Diagnostic data helps us find and fix bugs.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — authentication and encrypted cloud storage.</li>
      <li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> — subscription management.</li>
      <li><strong>App Store / Google Play</strong> — payment processing.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can export or delete your data at any time from in-app settings. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@envelope.app">privacy@envelope.app</a> for any request.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@envelope.app">privacy@envelope.app</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
